# ⚡ Chronos — A Study Planner by Team Privil

> **Your whole academic life, condensed into one clean black-and-white workspace.**
> No sign-ups. No backend. No bloat. Just open the file and start working.

🔗 **Live Demo:** [chronos-by-privil.netlify.app](https://chronos-by-privil.netlify.app/)

---

## 🎯 Why Chronos Exists

Most students juggle five separate apps just to stay organized — a to-do list, a calendar, a deadline tracker, a habit app, and a meditation app that never actually gets opened. Chronos merges all five into a single page, styled like an editorial design magazine rather than another SaaS dashboard.

It isn't trying to be "smart." It's trying to be **fast, honest, and free of distraction** — a workspace built to respect your attention instead of competing for it.

Built entirely with HTML, Tailwind, and vanilla JS. Clone it, open `index.html`, and it just works — no installs, no accounts, no setup.

---

## 🖤 Design Philosophy

Chronos leans into a deliberate **brutalist, architectural look**:

- **Pure black & white** — no color noise, no gradients, no visual clutter
- **Bebas Neue** for headers and numbers — bold, poster-style typography
- **Inter** for body copy — clean and easy to read
- **Thick 2px borders** in place of shadows or rounded corners, so the layout reads like ruled paper or a blueprint
- **Numbered sections (01–05)** instead of conventional tabs, like chapters in a book

The end result feels less like a productivity app and more like a **printed planner brought to life on screen.**

---

## 🧭 Walkthrough

### 01 — Work
Your daily command center.

- **Focus of the Day** — one oversized input at the top pushes you to name the single task that matters most today
- **Study Performance Dashboard** — a live stats panel tracking weekly completion, focus-goal percentage, and an editable "Agent Note" summarizing progress
- **Agent Plan** — a queue of AI-style suggested tasks (e.g. *"split Physics Pset 4 into two-hour blocks before Wednesday's lab"*) that you can accept or reject with one click, simulating an AI co-planner without needing a live API
- **Manual Tasks** — a classic checklist with satisfying strike-through animation on completion

### 02 — Week
A full **7-day agenda board**, Monday through Sunday, side by side.

- Add unlimited items to any day — just hit `Enter`
- Click any item to remove it instantly
- Weekend columns are subtly dimmed to visually separate study days from rest days

### 03 — Exams
Deadline and progress tracking for anything that affects your grade.

- Log exams, assignments, or projects, each with a clear type label
- Every entry gets a clickable progress bar that cycles 0% → 25% → 50% → 75% → 100% → reset — no sliders, no forms
- Built for at-a-glance scanning: title, type, and status all visible without opening anything

### 04 — Habits
Because grades aren't the only thing worth tracking.

- Add custom habits — water intake, reading, workouts, whatever matters to you
- Each habit keeps a live streak counter
- **Scratchpad** — a full-height, distraction-free notes panel for dumping thoughts without leaving the app
- **Daily Inspiration** button surfaces a full-screen motivational quote — click anywhere to dismiss

### 05 — Relax
Burnout isn't a strategy. A dedicated recovery suite:

| Tool | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Pomodoro Timer** | 25-minute work / 5-minute break cycles with play, pause, and reset |
| **4-7-8 Breathing** | A guided breathing circle that expands and contracts on a 4s inhale → 7s hold → 8s exhale loop |
| **5-4-3-2-1 Grounding** | An interactive sensory checklist for anxiety and stress reset |
| **Zen Focus** | A slow, morphing black-blob animation for ambient, screen-based meditation |

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Markup | HTML5 | Zero build tooling — works by just opening the file |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS (CDN) | Utility-first, no compiler step |
| Interactivity | Vanilla JavaScript | No framework overhead, nothing to break |
| Typography | Google Fonts — Bebas Neue + Inter | The editorial, poster-like identity |

**No npm install. No build step. No server. Just `index.html`.**

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

```bash
git clone https://github.com/minmon6767/Chronos-Workspace-Study-Agent.git
cd Chronos-Workspace-Study-Agent
```

Then either:

- **Double-click `index.html`** to open it in your browser, or
- **Serve it locally** for a cleaner dev experience:
  ```bash
  python3 -m http.server 8000
  ```
  Then visit `http://localhost:8000`

That's the whole process — no `npm install`, no `.env`, no config.

---

## 🌐 Deploying

Chronos is 100% static, so it can be live on the web in under two minutes on any static host — Netlify, Vercel, or GitHub Pages all work out of the box.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
chronos-workspace/
├── index.html      # The entire application — markup, styles, and logic
├── README.md       # You are here
├── LICENSE         # MIT
└── .gitignore
```

---

## 🔮 What's Next

Chronos currently runs in-memory, so refreshing the page resets your data. That's intentional for v1 — zero setup, zero accounts — but persistence (local storage or an optional account layer) is a natural next step.

Contributions and forks are welcome. This is meant to be a starting point, not a finished product.

